NAME
       gdisk - an interactive partition editor for GPT disks

SYNOPSIS
       gdisk DEVICE
       gdisk -l DEVICE

DESCRIPTION
       gdisk edits GPT partition tables with a one-letter menu much like
       fdisk. Nothing is written until w (which asks for confirmation); q
       leaves without saving. When gdisk opens a disk with an MBR table it
       offers to convert it to GPT in memory; that only happens if you then
       write.

       Partition types are four-digit hex codes: 8300 Linux filesystem (the
       default), 8200 Linux swap, 8e00 Linux LVM, 0700 Microsoft basic data,
       ef00 EFI system partition.

   Menu commands
       p      print the partition table
       n      new partition (number, first sector, last sector such as
              +1G, type code)
       d      delete a partition
       t      change a partition's type code
       l      list the type codes
       o      create a new, empty GPT table
       v      verify the disk
       ?      show the menu
       w      write the table and exit
       q      quit without saving

OPTIONS
       -l     Print the partition table and exit.

EXAMPLES
       A 2 GiB swap partition on /dev/vdc:

           gdisk /dev/vdc
           n, (Enter), (Enter), +2G, 8200
           w, y

SEE ALSO
       fdisk(8), parted(8), lsblk(8)
